## Approach

Single new file `src/moshier/backend.rs` containing four private helpers (`embofs_mosh`, `earth_position`, `helio_to_equatorial_j2000`, `moon_equatorial_j2000`) and a public `compute()` entry point that dispatches by `Body` variant. Pure functions throughout — obliquity and precession computed internally using default models. Planet speed uses backward difference (dt=0.0001 days); Moon speed uses second-order corrected central difference (dt=0.00005 days). Integration tested via C golden data generator calling `swe_calc` with all-corrections-disabled flags (+ XYZ for Cartesian output), comparing bitwise-exact (fallback to epsilon if computation-path ordering differs from swe_calc).

Alternative considered: calling internal C functions (swi_moshplan, swi_moshmoon) in the golden generator for tighter comparison, but rejected because those require global state setup (swed.oec) which complicates the standalone generator.

